<div class="home-container">
    <h1>Welcome to the Central Portal</h1>

    <p>
        This portal provides a unified place for community groups, councils, and local units 
        to organize their online presence. Whether you're managing a city-level group or a 
        single local unit, this system helps you create and maintain your site with ease.
    </p>

    <h2>How This Portal Works</h2>
    <p>
        The platform supports three levels of organization:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Global Portal Level</strong> – Oversees the entire system, manages settings, 
            and maintains all groups and units.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Group Level (City or Regional Councils)</strong> – Groups can manage their 
            own site and optionally oversee multiple local units within their area.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Local Unit Level</strong> – Individual units can create and manage their 
            own site, even if no group exists above them.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        This flexible structure allows units to operate independently or as part of a larger group.
    </p>

    <h2>Tools and Resources</h2>
    <p>
        The portal includes a collection of helpful tools designed for one-time or casual use. 
        These tools do not require creating a site or signing in, making them accessible to everyone.
    </p>

    <h2>Explore the Portal</h2>
    <p>
        Use the navigation above to browse unit sites, access tools, learn more about the system, 
        or sign in to manage your own site.
    </p>
</div>

